WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.980
Buying your first home can feel like a big step.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.120
It often begins before you have even found the right property.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.240
The first thing to understand is what you may be able to borrow.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:24.320
An adviser can help you explore what you may be able to borrow, based on your individual circumstances and lender criteria, and it helps to know that as you start looking.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.300
Mortgage Easy helps you get started.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.960
You can explore in your own time or book a conversation when you are ready.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:38.980
That technology means your adviser already understands your situation and can focus on what matters most.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.120
When choosing a mortgage, your adviser will help you explore options that may suit your circumstances.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.580
They can also help you prepare to make an offer.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:59.000
When the time is right, your adviser can provide an Agreement in Principle. An Agreement in Principle can help you prepare to make an offer — it is not a mortgage offer.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:05.560
From your initial application to completion, your adviser works with your conveyancer and estate agent.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.840
And when you finally open the door to your new home, it is your moment — and you will have felt more supported.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:13.480
Your journey.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.140
Made clearer.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.360
Understand what you may be able to borrow.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.620
Explore mortgage options with an adviser.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.240
Get your Agreement in Principle.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.940
Make your offer when you are ready.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.380
Move in — and talk about protecting what matters.
